{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794162771,"nonce":"0vO4h2K5ivNDosSzBmdIS+7b8zc=","message":"The mobile runners now present through the compositor, as the desktop runner does. The example no longer repaints the whole screen every frame.\n\nCause of the earlier full repaints: both runners called the direct path, `render_tree_with_motion`, which repaints the tree on every call. The compositor path needs a surface with COPY_DST and a runner that says when a frame may reuse the cached static layer.\n\nWhat changed:\n- `blinc_app::mobile_paint`: a shared \"needs a full paint\" flag. Input, text and key events, keyboard insets, rebuilds, stateful updates, scroll ticks, overlays and CSS state changes set it, and a full paint also runs when the last one is more than a second old.\n- iOS surface usage is RENDER_ATTACHMENT | COPY_DST. Android adds COPY_DST when `get_capabilities` lists it and otherwise stays on the direct path.\n- `apply_binding_deltas` returned false for a frame with no composite bindings once the dynamic batch carried the sticky `resolved` mark from cross-stream resolution. That invalidated the static layer every frame for any app with a canvas. It now returns true when the batch holds no foreground or ordered content (`PrimitiveBatch::has_ordered_content`).\n- `render_tree_with_motion_opt(.., try_fast_paint = false)` did not always repaint, because the compositor's inner call could reuse the cache. It now repaints.\n\nResults:\n- iPhone 12 Pro Max, example idle: GPU wait per frame 3.1 ms, against 12.5 to 13 ms with a full repaint each frame.\n- Emulator, final code: idle frames take the fast path 98% of the time, with one full repaint per second from the staleness guard. Zero rejected patches over taps, typing, a keyboard open and close, scroll and idle spinners. Counter, field text and focus ring, list scroll and the spinners all show the current frame.\n- blinc_app 353 of 353 with ignored GPU tests; blinc_gpu, blinc_layout, blinc_text, blinc_recorder and blinc_cn 1750 of 1750.\n\nNot checked yet: the iPhone with the final build, by the owner (no screen capture of the phone).","files":null}]}